.TH MU2EDAQ\-TEST\-ALL 1 "2026-07-23" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-test\-all \- test every mu2edaq\-* package built by mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-test\-all.sh
.RI [ package\ ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-test\-all.sh
runs the test suite of every package listed in the compatibility-test
manifest
.RI ( testing/common.sh ),
using the venvs and CMake build directories that
.B mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh
already produced. It is part of the
.B mu2edaq\-main
compatibility-test harness and is run from the root of the meta-repository.
.PP
For each package the following checks are performed, each recorded
independently and skipped (not failed) when not applicable to that package:
.IP \(bu 3
byte-compile every
.I .py
file with the package's venv interpreter (or the system interpreter for
script-only packages that have no venv);
.IP \(bu 3
import every dependency declared in
.I requirements.txt
plus any package-specific modules named in the manifest
.RI ( testing/smoke_imports.py );
.IP \(bu 3
.B bash \-n
every
.I .sh
file in the package;
.IP \(bu 3
run any CLI
.B \-\-help
smoke commands declared for the package, under a timeout, with
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen
so Qt/GUI packages do not need a display;
.IP \(bu 3
run the package's
.B pytest
suite, if the manifest names one, under a timeout;
.IP \(bu 3
run
.B ctest
against any CMake build directory that defines tests.
.PP
The script keeps going after a failure in one package, then writes a
markdown report summarizing the whole run, and exits non-zero if any package
failed.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.RI [ package\ ... ]
Test only the named package(s) instead of the full manifest. Unknown names
are skipped with a warning; this script takes no other options, so an
unrecognized flag is treated the same way.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.B .compat/status/test.tsv
One row per test step per package:
.IR pkg ", " step ", " "PASS/FAIL/SKIP" ", " logfile ", " timestamp .
Reset at the start of every run.
.TP
.B .compat/logs/test/
Full command output for every step, one log file per package/step.
.TP
.B .compat/report.md
Markdown report generated by
.B testing/report.py
from
.IR build.tsv " and " test.tsv ,
including log tails for every failure. Written even when some tests fail.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_PYTHON
Interpreter used where a package has no venv. Default:
.BR python3 .
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_COMPAT_DIR
Root directory for all harness artifacts (shared with
.BR mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh ).
Default:
.IR <repo\-root>/.compat .
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_SMOKE_TIMEOUT
Timeout in seconds for CLI smoke commands and the import-check step.
Default:
.BR 30 .
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_PYTEST_TIMEOUT
Timeout in seconds for each package's pytest run and for ctest.
Default:
.BR 600 .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every requested package's tests passed.
.TP
.B non-zero
At least one package failed at least one test step; the failing package
names are printed and the report is still written.
.SH EXAMPLES
Test everything and write the report:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-test\-all.sh
.EE
Test just one package:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-test\-all.sh mu2edaq\-fts
.EE
Shorter smoke/pytest timeouts for a quick local run:
.EX
    MU2EDAQ_SMOKE_TIMEOUT=10 MU2EDAQ_PYTEST_TIMEOUT=120 ./mu2edaq\-test\-all.sh
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-build\-all (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-setup\-env (1),
.BR pytest (1),
.BR ctest (1)
.SH REPOSITORY
.UR https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-main
https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-main
.UE
